<title>UK: Syndicate head Pisker leaves Lehman Brothers.</title>
<headline>Syndicate head Pisker leaves Lehman Brothers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andrew Pisker, global head of Fixed Income Syndicate, has left Lehman Brothers by mutual consent after 15 years with the firm, Lehman said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Pisker will be replaced by Glauco Cerri who will become head of credit businesses within its European fixed income division. Cerri joined Lehman earlier this year from CS First Boston.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
